 start+=panel('A few steps, then open your logbook','<ol class="steps"><li><h3>Choose the right network</h3><p>Create or select an RGN receiving address. In MetaMask, use the D14 network details below to see test rewards.</p></li><li><h3>Configure your miner</h3><p>Use the Stratum URL, your address.worker as username and x as password. No seed phrase or private key is ever needed by the pool.</p></li><li><h3>Watch accepted shares</h3><p>Give share statistics a few minutes to settle. Open Miners and search your address to see workers and accepted hashrate.</p></li><li><h3>Follow maturity and payouts</h3><p>RGN candidates must become canonical and mature before payment. DGB/DOGE wins depend on their separate network targets.</p></li></ol>')
 start+=panel('Hashpower rentals','<div class="two-grid"><div><h3>NiceHash or MiningRigRentals</h3><p>Select Scrypt, enter the Stratum host and port shown above, then use your RGN address.worker and password x for automatic share difficulty. A password such as x,d=2000000 requests a fixed preference; the pool may cap it lower to preserve block coverage. Check the rig’s requirements and verify the pool before renting.</p></div><div><h3>Difficulty and budget</h3><p>D14 starts at share difficulty 50,000 and automatically adjusts toward two seconds per share. The configured maximum is 2,000,000. A block-coverage cap may assign a lower value to preserve valid blocks on every active chain. Verify rig compatibility before renting; work does not guarantee a block or return.</p></div></div>')
 start+=panel('Wallet network','<dl class="detail-list" id="wallet-details"></dl><button class="button secondary" id="add-network" type="button">Add network to MetaMask '+icon('arrow')+'</button><p class="table-note" id="wallet-message" role="status">This D14 RPC supports read-only chain and balance requests. Transaction broadcasting is unavailable through this website. The wallet may ask you to confirm the network.</p>')
 start+=panel('Before you sail','<div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I need separate DGB and DOGE worker addresses?</summary><p>No. Your worker username is your RGN receiving address. Eligible DGB/DOGE mainnet rewards use the treasury destinations shown on the FORGE page.</p></details><details><summary>Does merged mining split my hashrate?</summary><p>The combined job reuses the same Scrypt work for eligible chains. Removing a chain does not automatically concentrate more hashes on another chain.</p></details><details><summary>Why can hashrate rise and fall?</summary><p>Pool hashrate is estimated from accepted shares over a time window. Rentals can also vary in delivered speed. Short windows fluctuate; compare accepted work over a longer period.</p></details><details><summary>Why is there no DGB or DOGE payout yet?</summary><p>An accepted share is easier than a network block. A qualifying proof still needs network acceptance and maturity. This website does not guarantee a block within a rental.</p></details></div>')

